            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-  Receptacles

-  Windows

-  Doors

-  Light fixtures

-  Electrical panel

-  Floor header joist

- Wood stove chimney

- Bathroom fan

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the time of the audit, the insulation was estimated to be R-28 (8.5?????????????????? of fiberglass insulation). We recommend the addition of insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. </ceilingsCathedral>
                <exposedFloors>The floor above the garage is considered as an exposed floor and could represent a big portion of your heat loss. A solution would be to increase the insulation and seal the floor to reduce air leakage. </exposedFloors>
                <foundation>Most of the heat loss in a home comes from the basement. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  </foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the basement wood window by triple pane and Energy Star certified unit with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>For more information concerning the Electrical Thermal Storage Unit, please follow the link below:

http://yukonconservation.org/programs/energy/electric-thermal-storage#:~:text=Electric%20thermal%20storage%20(ETS)%20is,providing%20heat%20throughout%20the%20day 

</AdditionalComments>
